# TargetCore wire formats that carry their own version, and the value each one
# is at. The versioning policy is the prose; this is the part a script can
# check.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The component version and the wire versions move
# INDEPENDENTLY and on purpose, so nothing about a release number tells you
# whether two peers can talk. That independence is right, and it has a cost:
# there is no single place a reviewer can look to see that a wire format moved.
# A one-character edit to `kVersion` in a .cpp is a decision to stop
# interoperating with every deployed peer, and before this file nothing
# anywhere would have reported it.
#
# A change here is therefore never incidental. Bump the constant and this file
# in the same commit, and say in that commit what stops talking to what.
#
# FORMAT: name  value  file  constant
# Checked by .github/ci/check_repo_invariants.py.
#
# NOT LISTED, because they have no version to check -- and their absence from
# this file is itself a fact worth being able to see:
#   GCM transport record (P2PeerioGcm)        -- nonce || ciphertext || tag
#   .p2p file image (Msgcore VBListBSTRio)    -- host byte order, undetected
#
# THE MESSAGE IMAGE USED TO BE ON THAT LIST AND IS NOT ANY MORE. It carries a
# LAYOUT GENERATION in the six sentinel bits of its oSync word -- currently 1
# (VBLock_SyncGenNow, 0xA4) -- so "32 bits, all spoken for" was true of the
# BITS and wrong about the consequence: the bits that were spent on a sentinel
# do the job of a version field, and the versioning policy now says so.
#
# IT IS STILL NOT A ROW HERE, and the reason is the same one C-2 cost a
# session to learn: the constant lives in Msgcore/Msgcore.h, in ANOTHER
# REPOSITORY, and a single-repository CI runner cannot resolve it. A row
# pointing there would fail as "does not exist" on every run, which is a check
# that reports the runner rather than the code. It is also a #define and not
# a `const ... = <n>;`, so the parser above would not read it either.
#
# WHAT CHECKS IT INSTEAD, and it is a stronger check than a grep: p2p_imagegen
# phase 0 asserts VBLock_SyncGenNow == VBLock_SyncGen1 against the library
# BUILT from that header, and phase 1 asserts that a frame the library has
# just serialised classifies as the current generation. A moved generation is
# a break of the same kind as a moved kVersion, so the same rule applies --
# say in the commit what stops talking to what.

login             2   P2PAuthLogin.cpp      kVersion
identity-store    1   P2PIdentityStore.cpp  kVersion
seal              2   P2PeerSeal.h          kSealVersion
